<title>JAPAN: JAPAN AVERAGE RATES ON TIME DEPOSITS.</title>
<headline>JAPAN AVERAGE RATES ON TIME DEPOSITS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to Aug 6 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.42 (0.44)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.50 (0.53)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.90 (0.95)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.38 (0.39)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.45 (0.48)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.31)	 three years  0.86 (0.90)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.33 (0.35)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.40 (0.43)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  0.81 (0.85)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Aug 4 - Aug 8:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.56 (0.59)   120-150 days  0.63 (0.65)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.57 (0.59)   150-180 days  0.66 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.63 (0.61)   180-360 days  0.71 (0.70)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.63 (0.66)   over 360 days 0.95 (1.40)</p>
